 "note": [
  "The English teen edition quotes the KJV; every epigraph is now the Louis Segond (1910) verse verbatim (French typographic spacing only) and the “(KJV)” label is dropped. Acts 3:19 in the KJV includes “times of refreshing”, which Segond places in 3:20, so the ch. 7 epigraph quotes Segond 3:19 + 3:20a and cites « Actes 3:19–20 »; 1 John 5:13 in Segond lacks the KJV’s closing “and that ye may believe…” clause, so the ch. 9 epigraph is shorter. Segond’s poetic capitals (« Pour s’éloigner », « D’abandonner », « J’aurai ») are kept in mined Jeremiah/Hosea quotations.",
  "Moody’s own sentences reuse the wording of the shipped French full edition « Le chemin vers Dieu » (vous-form kept inside his quotations; narration addresses the reader with « tu », as the other teen editions do); Moody’s death-bed saying reuses the French Moody biography. “Right about face” is « demi-tour ! » as in the full edition, which also gives the ch. 7 title « Demi-tour ! »; the count of “know” in 1 John is « savoir » / « Sache ! Sache !! SACHE !!! » as there.",
  "Names: Moody Bible Institute = « l’Institut biblique Moody »; “Little Hell” kept with a gloss « (le Petit Enfer) » as in the French bio; the publican is « publicain »; communion = « la cène ». Dollars kept (no conversion). Title « Le chemin vers Dieu (Pour ados) » is 31 characters — over the 28-char rail target, but it follows the full edition’s title and the shipped pattern (cf. « Une vie de confiance (Pour ados) », 32).",
  "Ch. 9: the English paraphrase of Spurgeon swaps his coney (« daman », Psalm 104:18) for a wild goat; the French follows the English (« chèvre sauvage ») — a native reviewer may prefer to restore the daman. Ch. 11 says Moody died in the room where he was born; this matches the house Moody bio and was left as is.",
  "QA 1 says Moody became a Christian at seventeen; he was born 5 February 1837 and converted 21 April 1855, i.e. at eighteen, so the French says « à dix-huit ans » (logged in english_errors). AI-translated in-session; awaiting native review."
 ],
